<title>RUSSIA: Russian Iraqi oil liftings up to 11.89 mln barrels.</title>
<headline>Russian Iraqi oil liftings up to 11.89 mln barrels.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian companies have lifted a total of 11.89 million barrels of the 26.23 million barrels of Iraqi crude oil for which they have contracts over a six-month period, a senior oil official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Yuri Agababov, deputy chief executive of Zarubezhneft, the company coordinating the contracts, said the increase came from Rosneft, which he said had lifted about 450,000 barrels from the Turkish Mediterranean port of Ceyhan.</p>
<p>Iraq began exporting oil in December 1996 under a $2 billion U.N. oil-for-food programme to raise cash for food and medicine. The seven Russian companies holding contracts with Baghdad account for nearly one quarter of all contracts approved so far.</p>
<p>-- Lynnley Browning, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
